                            <comment id="14999076" author="iveselovskiy" created="Tue, 10 Nov 2015 18:29:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/216&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/216&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14999081" author="iveselovskiy" created="Tue, 10 Nov 2015 18:31:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Relaxed slightly the logic of authority checking: if the URI authority does not containg IGFS name or Grid name, external (not embedded) connection is successful &amp;#8211; the IGFS owning this port is connected to. This is possible and is not contradictory because only one IGFS instance can be bound to a certain port.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15120953" author="vozerov" created="Thu, 28 Jan 2016 07:43:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi Ivan,&lt;br/&gt;
I found the following problems in implementation:&lt;br/&gt;
1) IgfsIpcHandler.processHandshakeRequest - what is &quot;req.gridName() != null&quot; check for?&lt;br/&gt;
2) I believe we do not need &quot;PARAM_IGFS_ENDPOINT_NO_REMOTE_TCP&quot; property. What is it for? If user specified remote host then he definitely want to connect to remote host if other optimization attempts failed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15219908" author="iveselovskiy" created="Thu, 31 Mar 2016 14:11:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;1) req.gridName() != null &amp;amp; req.igfsName() != null checks are needed to check the grid &amp;amp; igfs names only if some non-empty names are requested. Otherwize the default ones will be used in TCP modes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2) fixed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;3) Also I changed the logic so that connection to local address is not made if the specified address is remote.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15221611" author="iveselovskiy" created="Fri, 1 Apr 2016 12:08:47 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;as earlier, pull request  &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/216&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/216&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15227062" author="vozerov" created="Tue, 5 Apr 2016 20:17:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ivan,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix is invalid. You cannot disable local instance check because this is absolutely valid scenario.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;E.g. user work with &quot;igfs://somehost&quot;. &quot;somehost&quot; - is a node with IPC handler, nothing more. Then user submit a job to a cluster with 20 nodes. Each node has the same IGFS instance running, but has different host name. Do you really want to disable optimization with local instance for all these nodes?  I guess no.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;All these changes must be reverted back. The only thing to be changed is error handling.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15235126" author="iveselovskiy" created="Mon, 11 Apr 2016 14:06:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;fixed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15237110" author="githubbot" created="Tue, 12 Apr 2016 13:01:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user asfgit closed the pull request at:&lt;/p&gt;

